{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "model": "SidecarUndo",
  "assumptions": [
    "One fixed-address deleted image and at most one competing insert.",
    "The delete log record is durable before the modified page can survive a crash.",
    "Recovery removes a durable losing competitor before deletion undo. The necessity and engine ordering are unproved.",
    "A dirty competitor insert survives a crash only if its log record is durable.",
    "The proposed latch or reservation blocks deallocation before end append. Page deallocation after end append and its WAL and restart semantics are excluded.",
    "Both reservation and latch policies are proposed guards, not established engine behavior."
  ],
